{title: Joyful, Joyful, We Adore Thee}
{artist: Henry van Dyke & Ludwig van Beethoven}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 100}

Verse 1
[G]Joyful, joyful, [D]we adore thee, [G]God of glory, [D]Lord of [G]love;
hearts unfold like [D]flowers before thee, [G]opening to the [D]sun a[G]bove.
[D]Melt the clouds of [G]sin and [D]sadness, [G]drive the [D]dark of [A]doubt a[D]way;
[G]giver of im[D]mortal gladness, [G]fill us with the [D]light of [G]day.

Verse 2
[G]All Thy [D]works with joy [G]surround Thee, earth [D]and heaven [G]reflect
Thy rays, Stars [D]and angels sing [G]around Thee, center [D]of unbroken
[D]praise. Field and [G]forest, vale [D]and [G]mountain, flowery [D]meadow, [A]flashing sea,
[G]Singing bird and flowing [G]fountain call us to [D]rejoice in [G]Thee.

Verse 3
[G]Thou art [D]giving and forgiving, [G]ever blessing, ever [D]blessed, Wellspring [G]of
the joy of [D]living, ocean depth [G]of happy rest! [D]Thou our
[D]Father, Christ our Brother, [G]all who [D]live [G]in love [D]are Thine; [A]Teach us
[G]how to love each [G]other, lift us to [D]the joy [G]divine.

Verse 4
[G]Mortals, join [D]the happy chorus, [G]which the morning [D]stars began; [G]Father
love is reigning [D]o'er us, brother [G]love binds man [D]to man.
[D]Ever singing, march [G]we onward, [D]victors [G]in the [D]midst [A]of strife,
[G]Joyful music leads us [G]Sunward in the triumph [D]song of [G]life.
